# .dockerignore — Excludes files from the Docker build context
#
# When you run `docker build` or `docker compose up --build`, Docker sends
# the entire project directory to the Docker daemon as the "build context".
# Files listed here are excluded from that transfer.
#
# Why this matters:
#   1. Speed     — Smaller context = faster upload to the daemon
#   2. Cache     — Prevents irrelevant file changes from busting the layer cache
#   3. Security  — Keeps secrets and local config out of the image
#   4. Size      — node_modules alone can be 200MB+; we rebuild inside Docker

# ── Node.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Vite build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# We rebuild inside Docker; local /dist should never be copied in
dist/
dist-ssr/

# ── Environment files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env may contain real secrets — keep it out of the image
.env
*.local

# ── Git history ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Editor / OS artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Documentation & Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
*.md
